Package: coreval
Title: Evaluate CDISC Open Rules (CORE) Conformance Against Clinical Trial Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Hrach", "Gevorgyan", email = "hrach.gevorgyan@yandex.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Checks clinical trial datasets against the CDISC Open Rules
    (CORE) conformance rules and returns the findings as a tidy data frame,
    so data issues can be found and fixed early rather than late. Intended
    as a fast, local, unqualified pre-check that runs alongside - never
    instead of - a qualified validation system. Reads study data from
    transport ('XPT'), 'SAS' and comma-separated files, and reads a
    Define-XML file when one is present. Covers rules for the SDTM, SEND and
    TIG standards across their published versions. Rule definitions are
    bundled as data, extracted at build time from a pinned commit of the
    CDISC Open Rules repository, so checking a study needs no internet
    connection, no API key and no external service. Rules that cannot be
    evaluated are reported as skipped, with a reason, rather than silently
    passing. An independent project: not affiliated with or endorsed by
    CDISC, and not a CORE-certified conformance engine.
